 **Open question OQ-1 — API language:** Node/Fastify (one language with the UI, 2 languages total with Java tracer) vs Java (e.g., Javalin; one backend language, but a second ecosystem beside TS). **Default: Node/Fastify.** Decide in [[Phase 0 - Setup]]; record the outcome here.
 
+**OQ-1 OUTCOME (2026-11-14, Phase 0):** ✅ Decided — **Node 20 + Fastify**. Rationale: shares the TS toolchain/lint/CI pipeline with the web app, trivial container-spawning ergonomics (`child_process`), and the tracer's Java dependency does not force a JVM on the API anyway. Recorded also in `runflow/services/api/README.md`.
+
 **Licensing note:** check licenses of all dependencies (e.g., ELKjs is EPL-2.0 if adopted; JavaParser LGPL/Apache dual) before launch ([[Public Launch Gate]]).
 Related: [[Tech Stack]], [[Frontend Architecture]].
diff --git a/runflow/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/runflow/.github/workflows/ci.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3b38897
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runflow/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+name: CI
+on:
+  push:
+  pull_request:
+jobs:
+  web:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    defaults: { run: { working-directory: apps/web } }
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+        with: { node-version: 20, cache: npm, cache-dependency-path: apps/web/package-lock.json }
+      - run: npm ci
+      - run: npm run lint
+      - run: npx tsc --noEmit
+      - run: npm run build
+      - run: npm audit --omit=dev
+  corpus:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-java@v4
+        with: { distribution: temurin, java-version: 17 }
+      - name: Compile DSA corpus
+        run: for f in testcorpus/dsa/*/Main.java; do javac -d /tmp/out "$f"; done
+      - name: Validate golden/fake traces against schema
+        run: |
+          pip install jsonschema
+          python -c "
+          import json,glob
+          from jsonschema import Draft202012Validator
+          s=json.load(open('schemas/trace.schema.json'))
+          v=Draft202012Validator(s)
+          files=glob.glob('testcorpus/golden/*.json')
+          assert files, 'no trace files found'
+          for f in files:
+              errs=list(v.iter_errors(json.load(open(f))))
+              print(f, 'OK' if not errs else errs[0].message)
+              assert not errs, f
+          "
